## 4. Practical Scripting with MRVS Data

Because MRVS stores data as a JSON string, client and server scripts must serialize and deserialize the content when reading or updating rows.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

| Multi-Row Variable Set (MRVS Interface)                                           |

+-------------------+--------------------+--------------------+---------------------+

| Target System     | Access Role        | Justification      | Actions             |

+-------------------+--------------------+--------------------+---------------------+

| SAP ERP           | Financial Reviewer | Quarterly audit    | [ Edit ] [ Delete ] |

| Salesforce CRM    | Sales Rep          | New team transfer  | [ Edit ] [ Delete ] |

+-------------------+--------------------+--------------------+---------------------+

| [ Add Row ]                                                                       |

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

### Client-Side Example: Reading MRVS Data (Catalog Client Script)

JavaScript

function onSubmit() {

// Fetch JSON string from MRVS internal name

```javascript
var mrvsData = g_form.getValue('access_entitlements_mrvs');
```

if (mrvsData && mrvsData !== '[]') {

```javascript
var rows = JSON.parse(mrvsData);
```

// Enforce business rule: At least one row must be added

if (rows.length < 1) {

```javascript
g_form.addErrorMessage('Please add at least one entitlement row before submitting.');
```

return false;

}

}

}

### Server-Side Example: Processing MRVS in Flow Designer / Script Include

JavaScript

// Server-side script reading MRVS from RITM record

```javascript
var ritmGr = new GlideRecord('sc_req_item');
```

if (ritmGr.get('SYS_ID_OF_RITM')) {

var jsonString = ritmGr.variables.access_entitlements_mrvs;

```javascript
var rowList = JSON.parse(jsonString);
```

for (var i = 0; i < rowList.length; i++) {

var systemName = rowList[i].target_system;

var role = rowList[i].access_role;

```javascript
gs.info('Processing row ' + (i + 1) + ': System=' + systemName + ', Role=' + role);
```

}

}

### 5. Typical Real-World Use Cases

Bulk Asset / Hardware Requests: A manager orders monitors, keyboards, and headsets for 5 new hires in a single catalog submission.

Access & Role Allocations: Requesting multiple system entitlements (e.g., Active Directory groups, SAP roles) with distinct justifications per row.

Travel Expense Estimates: Itemizing hotel, flight, and daily meal allowances within a travel authorization request item.

