## 4. Asynchronous Server Calls via GlideAjax

GlideAjax allows client-side scripts to call server-side Script Include methods asynchronously using sysparm parameters, fetching data dynamically without freezing the user browser.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

|                            GlideAjax Communication Flow                           |

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

|  1. User changes field value (e.g., 'Requested For' user)                         |

|     │                                                                             |

|     ▼                                                                             |

|  2. Catalog Client Script builds GlideAjax request with sysparm parameters         |

|     │                                                                             |

|     ▼                                                                             |

|  3. Server executes Script Include method (extends AbstractScriptInclude)         |

|     │                                                                             |

|     ▼                                                                             |

|  4. Server sends response back to client callback function (getXMLAnswer)        |

|     │                                                                             |

|     ▼                                                                             |

|  5. Form fields auto-populate dynamically without page refresh                    |

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+

### 5. End-to-End GlideAjax Implementation Example

### Step A: Script Include (Server-Side)

### Name: CatalogDataEvaluator

### Client callable: Check box true (Mandatory)

JavaScript

var CatalogDataEvaluator = Class.create();

CatalogDataEvaluator.prototype = Object.extendsObject(AbstractScriptInclude, {

getUserDetails: function() {

var userId = this.getParameter('sysparm_user_id');

var result = {

email: '',

phone: '',

department: ''

};

if (userId) {

```javascript
var userGr = new GlideRecord('sys_user');
```

if (userGr.get(userId)) {

result.email = userGr.getValue('email') || '';

result.phone = userGr.getValue('phone') || '';

result.department = userGr.department.getDisplayValue() || '';

}

}

// Convert object to JSON string for client-side parsing

return JSON.stringify(result);

},

type: 'CatalogDataEvaluator'

});

### Step B: Catalog Client Script (Client-Side)

### Type: onChange

### Variable Name: requested_for

JavaScript

function onChange(control, oldValue, newValue, isLoading, isTemplate) {

if (isLoading || newValue === '') {

```javascript
g_form.clearValue('email');
```

```javascript
g_form.clearValue('phone');
```

```javascript
g_form.clearValue('department');
```

return;

}

// Initialize GlideAjax instance with Script Include Name

var ga = new GlideAjax('CatalogDataEvaluator');

ga.addParam('sysparm_name', 'getUserDetails'); // Method to invoke

ga.addParam('sysparm_user_id', newValue);      // Target payload parameter

// Send request asynchronously and pass callback function

ga.getXMLAnswer(function(response) {

if (response) {

```javascript
var userData = JSON.parse(response);
```

// Auto-populate target catalog variables

```javascript
g_form.setValue('email', userData.email);
```

```javascript
g_form.setValue('phone', userData.phone);
```

```javascript
g_form.setValue('department', userData.department);
```

}

});

}

